WEBVTT

1
00:00:34,769 --> 00:00:36,738
(ETHEREAL MUSIC PLAYING)

2
00:00:52,587 --> 00:00:55,557
BART: <i>I found a song</i>
<i>that saved me through time.</i>

3
00:00:57,357 --> 00:01:00,394
<i>A song that opened my life</i>
<i>up to things</i>

4
00:01:00,427 --> 00:01:02,362
<i>I couldn't have</i>
<i>possibly imagined.</i>

5
00:01:04,766 --> 00:01:06,300
<i>It made me believe that...</i>

6
00:01:07,802 --> 00:01:09,269
<i>That dreams do come true.</i>

7
00:01:10,437 --> 00:01:12,674
(CROWD CHEERING)

8
00:01:12,707 --> 00:01:14,676
<i>I dreamed of something good</i>

9
00:01:14,709 --> 00:01:16,511
<i>with my dad before he died,</i>

10
00:01:17,244 --> 00:01:18,746
<i>of being a good husband,</i>

11
00:01:19,179 --> 00:01:21,549
<i>a good father,</i>

12
00:01:21,583 --> 00:01:24,652
<i>of writing songs that could</i>
<i>touch the hearts of millions</i>

13
00:01:25,620 --> 00:01:28,188
<i>with the same hope</i>
<i>that music gave to me.</i>

14
00:01:30,658 --> 00:01:32,125
<i>And it all came true.</i>

15
00:01:33,595 --> 00:01:34,461
<i>But what comes next</i>

16
00:01:34,494 --> 00:01:36,196
<i>when you've gotten</i>
<i>all your dreams?</i>

17
00:01:37,331 --> 00:01:39,132
<i>After all</i>
<i>the applause dies down</i>

18
00:01:39,166 --> 00:01:41,435
<i>and the crowds go home,</i>

19
00:01:41,468 --> 00:01:43,871
<i>is there life</i>
<i>after the happily-ever-after?</i>

20
00:01:45,105 --> 00:01:46,641
<i>When it all gets hard again,</i>

21
00:01:48,375 --> 00:01:50,444
<i>when the pain never seems</i>
<i>to go away?</i>

22
00:01:52,947 --> 00:01:55,282
<i>What do you do</i>
<i>when the only thing</i>

23
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:57,685
<i>in the whole world</i>
<i>you have to hold on to</i>

24
00:01:58,553 --> 00:01:59,621
<i>is a song?</i>

25
00:02:00,922 --> 00:02:03,691
(UPLIFTING MUSIC PLAYING)

26
00:02:26,146 --> 00:02:27,347
SHANNON: Hey, Bart,
the bus is here.

27
00:02:27,381 --> 00:02:28,516
I just got Gracie down
for a nap.

28
00:02:28,549 --> 00:02:29,784
-(SHUSHING)
-You about ready

29
00:02:29,817 --> 00:02:30,818
to leave or no?

30
00:02:31,719 --> 00:02:32,720
SHANNON: (SOFTLY) Ah.

31
00:02:33,721 --> 00:02:35,155
BART: Well, dang.

32
00:02:36,057 --> 00:02:37,792
Bummer. I mean,
I was really hoping

33
00:02:37,825 --> 00:02:39,493
to see Sam before I left.

34
00:02:39,527 --> 00:02:40,795
SHANNON: I wonder where he is.

35
00:02:42,429 --> 00:02:44,297
I was gonna let him borrow
my Nano.

36
00:02:44,331 --> 00:02:47,135
Loaded up some sweet new U2,

37
00:02:47,167 --> 00:02:49,070
-some Jars...
-Whoa.

38
00:02:49,103 --> 00:02:50,938
...big band.

39
00:02:50,972 --> 00:02:53,007
-(TUTS AND SIGHS)
-Oh, well.

40
00:02:53,041 --> 00:02:54,575
Too bad he's not here.

41
00:02:54,609 --> 00:02:55,877
Yes,

42
00:02:55,910 --> 00:02:58,613
that is too bad.

43
00:03:08,255 --> 00:03:09,456
(BOTH CHUCKLE)

44
00:03:12,660 --> 00:03:13,728
Hey, big man.

45
00:03:14,461 --> 00:03:16,296
You wanna talk about it?

46
00:03:16,329 --> 00:03:19,499
Why do you always miss
the good stuff?

47
00:03:19,534 --> 00:03:21,703
-(CHUCKLES UNCOMFORTABLY)
-SHANNON: Buddy,

48
00:03:21,736 --> 00:03:24,204
your dad's out
working for us, Sam.

49
00:03:24,237 --> 00:03:26,908
But yeah, I'll miss him, too.

50
00:03:26,941 --> 00:03:28,442
I'll be back in two days,
okay?

51
00:03:28,475 --> 00:03:30,712
And then you and me,
maybe we could... Oh.

52
00:03:32,947 --> 00:03:34,481
What should we listen to?

53
00:03:35,215 --> 00:03:36,450
Here, you pick.

54
00:03:42,322 --> 00:03:43,457
(BUTTON CLICKS)

55
00:03:43,490 --> 00:03:45,860
<i>(I CAN ONLY IMAGINE</i>
BY MERCYME PLAYING)

56
00:03:57,370 --> 00:03:59,640
MAN ON RADIO:
I Can Only Imagine <i>by MercyMe,</i>

57
00:03:59,674 --> 00:04:02,309
<i>one of the most beloved songs</i>
<i>of all time</i>

58
00:04:02,342 --> 00:04:04,145
<i>shows no signs</i>
<i>of slowing down.</i>

59
00:04:04,178 --> 00:04:05,646
WOMAN ON RADIO:
<i>As MercyMe's surprise hit</i>

60
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:08,216
I Can Only Imagine
<i>shook the world</i>

61
00:04:08,248 --> 00:04:09,517
<i>and went double platinum.</i>

62
00:04:09,550 --> 00:04:11,119
MAN 2 ON RADIO: <i>Here it is,</i>
<i>by popular demand,</i>

63
00:04:11,152 --> 00:04:13,154
<i>the song that everyone is</i>
<i>talking about,</i>

64
00:04:13,187 --> 00:04:15,556
<i>coming in this week</i>
<i>at number one.</i>

65
00:04:15,590 --> 00:04:17,290
WOMAN 2:
...I Can Only Imagine.

66
00:04:17,324 --> 00:04:18,559
WOMAN 3: <i>This group reached</i>
<i>number four</i>

67
00:04:18,593 --> 00:04:20,995
<i>on the Adult</i>
<i>Contemporary radio charts</i>

68
00:04:21,028 --> 00:04:24,232
<i>and soared to number one</i>
<i>in Christian Radio.</i>

69
00:04:24,264 --> 00:04:25,900
<i>Here's MercyMe.</i>

70
00:04:27,034 --> 00:04:28,035
All right.

71
00:04:30,505 --> 00:04:32,673
ANNOUNCER: It's such an honor
to announce the nominees

72
00:04:32,707 --> 00:04:34,776
for the best
Christian Artist of the year.

73
00:04:34,809 --> 00:04:36,309
You boys better have
that money ready.

74
00:04:36,343 --> 00:04:37,645
If we win, I'm doin' it.

75
00:04:37,678 --> 00:04:40,380
What exactly are we doing,
Bartholomew?

76
00:04:40,413 --> 00:04:42,850
(CHUCKLES) He's gotta use
whatever we write

77
00:04:42,884 --> 00:04:43,885
in his speech.

78
00:04:43,918 --> 00:04:45,653
And he can't look at it
till he gets on stage.

79
00:04:45,686 --> 00:04:47,855
I'm so not comfortable
with this.

80
00:04:47,889 --> 00:04:49,824
ALL: Shut up, Robby.

81
00:04:49,857 --> 00:04:51,291
Oh, man, I hope we lose.

82
00:04:51,324 --> 00:04:52,593
And the winner is

83
00:04:52,627 --> 00:04:56,329
MercyMe
for <i>I Can Only Imagine!</i> Woo!

84
00:04:56,363 --> 00:04:58,431
(AUDIENCE CHEERING)

85
00:04:58,465 --> 00:05:00,735
<i>♪ Will I dance for You, Jesus</i>

86
00:05:00,768 --> 00:05:04,272
<i>♪ Or in awe of You</i>
<i>be still? ♪</i>

87
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:05,472
BART: Who am I kiddin'?

88
00:05:05,506 --> 00:05:07,307
I'm just a kid
from Greenville, Texas,

89
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:08,910
you know.

90
00:05:11,913 --> 00:05:13,014
(CHUCKLING) I...

91
00:05:13,047 --> 00:05:16,083
My meemaw used to say to me,
she'd say, "Pickles..."

92
00:05:16,117 --> 00:05:17,350
(MEN LAUGHING FAINTLY)

93
00:05:17,384 --> 00:05:18,753
Pickles was
her nickname for me.

94
00:05:18,786 --> 00:05:20,188
-(AUDIENCE LAUGHS FAINTLY)
-BART: It's very endearing.

95
00:05:20,221 --> 00:05:21,889
Um, and she would say

96
00:05:21,923 --> 00:05:25,425
"Sometimes, happily-ever-afters
do come true."

97
00:05:25,458 --> 00:05:27,628
But then she'd say,
"Don't bet on it.
Get a real job."

98
00:05:27,662 --> 00:05:28,963
-You know? So...
-(AUDIENCE CHUCKLING)

99
00:05:28,996 --> 00:05:30,531
Um...

100
00:05:30,565 --> 00:05:33,433
Meemaw, God is good.
Dreams do come true.

101
00:05:33,466 --> 00:05:35,670
Thank you so much, everyone.
Have a great night.

102
00:05:36,436 --> 00:05:38,773
(ALL CHEERING)

103
00:05:45,646 --> 00:05:48,149
All right. Easy money, boys.
Easy money.

104
00:05:48,182 --> 00:05:49,449
Ah, thank you.

105
00:05:49,482 --> 00:05:50,785
-(PHONE VIBRATING)
-BART: Ooh.

106
00:05:52,186 --> 00:05:53,287
-Hey.
-SHANNON: <i>Hi, I just thought</i>

107
00:05:53,321 --> 00:05:54,755
<i>-I'd check in on ya.</i>
-We won.

108
00:05:54,789 --> 00:05:57,024
SHANNON: Again? (LAUGHING)
I'm so proud of you guys!

109
00:05:57,058 --> 00:05:59,627
-Babe! That's awesome.
<i>-Yeah, we're gonna have</i>

110
00:05:59,660 --> 00:06:01,428
<i>to take another box</i>
<i>of these things to storage</i>

111
00:06:01,461 --> 00:06:02,563
<i>if we keep winning.</i>

112
00:06:02,597 --> 00:06:04,165
I'm glad one of us is winning.

113
00:06:04,198 --> 00:06:05,800
<i>Sounds like World War III.</i>

114
00:06:05,833 --> 00:06:08,903
-That would somehow be easier.
-(KIDS YELLING)

115
00:06:08,936 --> 00:06:10,605
Hey, I know Sam wanted
to talk to you.

116
00:06:10,638 --> 00:06:13,307
Sam, you wanna talk to Daddy?
Here you go.

117
00:06:13,341 --> 00:06:15,243
-Hey, Dad.
<i>-Hey, Sam.</i>

118
00:06:15,276 --> 00:06:16,677
How's the party going?

119
00:06:16,711 --> 00:06:18,179
Are you having fun, big man?

120
00:06:18,212 --> 00:06:19,379
I barfed.

121
00:06:19,412 --> 00:06:20,948
Is that right? Um...

122
00:06:20,982 --> 00:06:22,449
I won the costume contest.

123
00:06:22,482 --> 00:06:24,352
<i>Oh, that's great, bud.</i>

124
00:06:24,417 --> 00:06:25,753
Ah, man, I bet
you were a great Legolas.

125
00:06:25,786 --> 00:06:27,655
Um, the bow and arrow,
how's your aim?

126
00:06:27,688 --> 00:06:29,523
I shot the white lamp
and it broke

127
00:06:29,557 --> 00:06:31,726
so Mommy took it away.

128
00:06:31,759 --> 00:06:33,361
I never cared for that lamp.

129
00:06:33,393 --> 00:06:35,162
SHANNON: <i>All right, Sam.</i>
<i>Say bye to Daddy.</i>

130
00:06:35,196 --> 00:06:36,364
SAM: <i>Bye, Daddy. I love you.</i>

131
00:06:36,396 --> 00:06:38,532
I love you too, big man.

132
00:06:38,566 --> 00:06:42,103
Hi. I'm back.
I'm outta gas, man.

133
00:06:42,136 --> 00:06:43,371
BART: <i>Hang in there, Shannon.</i>

134
00:06:43,403 --> 00:06:45,973
Just another tour,
couple more albums

135
00:06:46,007 --> 00:06:47,074
<i>and we're gonna be set.</i>

136
00:06:47,108 --> 00:06:49,877
You know, I think
that's what you said
last tour.

137
00:06:49,911 --> 00:06:51,646
Yeah, that's fair. Um...

138
00:06:51,679 --> 00:06:54,382
And great. Someone gave
Sam back his bow and arrow.

139
00:06:54,414 --> 00:06:56,083
I gotta go. Love you, Millard.

140
00:06:56,117 --> 00:06:57,484
You too, M...

141
00:06:59,253 --> 00:07:00,788
(HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING)

142
00:07:27,415 --> 00:07:29,417
(RADIO STATIC BUZZING)

143
00:07:29,449 --> 00:07:31,986
ARTHUR: <i>I want you</i>
<i>to go chase your dream.</i>

144
00:07:32,019 --> 00:07:33,354
(INAUDIBLE)

145
00:07:33,387 --> 00:07:35,523
And I want you to catch it.

146
00:07:36,057 --> 00:07:37,224
BART: <i>I promise.</i>

147
00:07:45,433 --> 00:07:47,068
I caught my dream, Dad.

148
00:07:51,806 --> 00:07:52,873
I miss you.

149
00:07:53,941 --> 00:07:55,710
(PHONE VIBRATING)

150
00:07:59,479 --> 00:08:00,514
Hey, babe.

151
00:08:00,548 --> 00:08:01,916
SHANNON:
(VOICE SHAKING) <i>Bart?</i>

152
00:08:01,949 --> 00:08:04,352
-Shannon, what's going on?
<i>-I can't get Sam to wake up.</i>

153
00:08:04,385 --> 00:08:06,153
-What?
<i>-I can't get Sam to wake up!</i>

154
00:08:11,993 --> 00:08:13,527
WOMAN: Hey, baby, Mommy
and Daddy are here, okay?

155
00:08:13,561 --> 00:08:15,062
-NURSE: Coming through.
-We're all right here for you.

156
00:08:15,096 --> 00:08:16,998
You just need to keep
breathing for me, okay?

157
00:08:17,031 --> 00:08:19,033
Everything is gonna be okay.
You're okay.

158
00:08:19,066 --> 00:08:20,634
No, no, I've gotta...

159
00:08:21,969 --> 00:08:22,970
Okay.

160
00:08:29,744 --> 00:08:30,678
Hi.

161
00:08:30,711 --> 00:08:32,113
-Hey!
-I'm here, baby.

162
00:08:32,146 --> 00:08:33,647
(CRYING SOFTLY)

163
00:08:35,916 --> 00:08:36,917
BART: I'm here.

164
00:08:37,551 --> 00:08:39,120
What, um...

165
00:08:39,153 --> 00:08:41,555
(SHANNON CRYING)

166
00:08:41,589 --> 00:08:42,790
What happened?

167
00:08:43,391 --> 00:08:46,160
He had a, a seizure,

168
00:08:46,193 --> 00:08:47,228
(SIGHS) or something,

169
00:08:47,261 --> 00:08:50,097
and now they can't get him
to wake up. (SNIFFLES)

170
00:08:50,131 --> 00:08:51,632
I don't really know.

171
00:08:53,100 --> 00:08:54,535
(SIGHS) Bart, I'm scared.

172
00:08:54,568 --> 00:08:56,037
-(SNIFFLES)
-I know, I know.

173
00:08:57,338 --> 00:08:58,606
Me too.

174
00:08:59,874 --> 00:09:02,576
WOMAN ON PA:
<i>Paging Dr. Lund, line 3.</i>

175
00:09:02,610 --> 00:09:04,311
<i>Dr. Lund, line 3.</i>

176
00:09:14,155 --> 00:09:16,190
SAM: Mama, I'm thirsty.

177
00:09:18,359 --> 00:09:19,927
Hi!

178
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,862
Baby!

179
00:09:21,896 --> 00:09:23,731
Baby, hi!

180
00:09:23,764 --> 00:09:24,965
BART: <i>Right. So we just</i>

181
00:09:24,999 --> 00:09:27,768
<i>lower his sugar intake,</i>
<i>and then what?</i>

182
00:09:27,802 --> 00:09:29,670
He's got to lose some weight
or something, right?

183
00:09:29,703 --> 00:09:32,106
No. Once again,
that is Type 2 diabetes.

184
00:09:32,139 --> 00:09:34,108
Your son has Type 1.

185
00:09:35,576 --> 00:09:38,746
This insulin is life support.

186
00:09:39,313 --> 00:09:41,882
Sam's glucose was 840.

187
00:09:41,916 --> 00:09:44,051
That's 10 times
the normal range.

188
00:09:44,852 --> 00:09:45,853
There's another kid here

189
00:09:45,886 --> 00:09:47,021
that's slightly higher
than him

190
00:09:47,054 --> 00:09:48,789
that we haven't been able
to stabilize yet.

191
00:09:48,823 --> 00:09:50,057
And if you would have
gotten him here any later,

192
00:09:50,091 --> 00:09:52,726
Sam would have been
in the exact same position.

193
00:09:52,760 --> 00:09:55,229
I wish
it could be different,

194
00:09:55,262 --> 00:09:56,797
but this is Sam's life now.

195
00:09:58,099 --> 00:09:59,166
It's yours, too.

196
00:10:02,803 --> 00:10:05,372
(BART INHALES
AND EXHALES DEEPLY)

197
00:10:07,641 --> 00:10:10,211
SAM: Do we have to, Daddy?

198
00:10:10,244 --> 00:10:11,745
(LANCET CLICKS)

199
00:10:12,713 --> 00:10:14,815
BURT: (SIGHS) Yeah, buddy.
Um...

200
00:10:15,449 --> 00:10:16,750
I'm afraid we do.

201
00:10:18,419 --> 00:10:20,221
I need your finger, okay?

202
00:10:20,921 --> 00:10:22,423
SAM: Okay.

203
00:10:22,456 --> 00:10:24,391
-(LANCET CLICKS)
-BART: Okay, bud.

204
00:10:26,227 --> 00:10:27,828
SAM: Wait, wait, wait.

205
00:10:28,662 --> 00:10:31,332
What do you do
when you're scared?

206
00:10:37,304 --> 00:10:38,839
(INHALES AND EXHALE SHARPLY)

207
00:10:40,074 --> 00:10:41,675
I think everything's
a little less scary

208
00:10:41,709 --> 00:10:43,244
with a friend, right?

209
00:10:48,315 --> 00:10:49,316
Watch me.

210
00:10:50,017 --> 00:10:51,018
(LANCET CLICKS)

211
00:10:52,786 --> 00:10:54,623
That's not so bad.

212
00:10:54,655 --> 00:10:55,923
Okay?

213
00:10:56,957 --> 00:10:58,692
It just stings a little bit.

214
00:10:59,927 --> 00:11:01,428
You wanna pick out a song?

215
00:11:02,631 --> 00:11:03,864
Okay.

216
00:11:04,665 --> 00:11:06,000
Pick a good one.

217
00:11:07,067 --> 00:11:08,135
(INHALES)

218
00:11:13,741 --> 00:11:15,544
<i>(40</i> BY U2 PLAYING)

219
00:11:15,577 --> 00:11:16,777
Good choice.

220
00:11:18,245 --> 00:11:19,413
Okay, buddy.

221
00:11:22,349 --> 00:11:23,552
-(LANCET CLICKS)
-(WINCES)

222
00:11:23,585 --> 00:11:24,718
Hey, hey, it's okay.

223
00:11:24,752 --> 00:11:26,053
-It's okay. It's okay.
-Good job.

224
00:11:27,388 --> 00:11:28,822
(SIGHS)

225
00:11:28,856 --> 00:11:30,157
(GLUCOSE METER BEEPS)

226
00:11:32,627 --> 00:11:33,827
All right, buddy.

227
00:11:36,964 --> 00:11:38,533
-(SAM WINCES)
-SHANNON: Yep. You're okay.

228
00:11:38,567 --> 00:11:40,669
-BART: Okay.
-(SAM CRYING)

229
00:11:40,701 --> 00:11:42,403
-You're hurting me.
-SHANNON: It's okay.

230
00:11:42,436 --> 00:11:44,405
-Daddy's just trying to help.
-(TABLE THUDS LOUDLY)

231
00:11:44,438 --> 00:11:46,840
BART: Get away from me!

232
00:11:46,874 --> 00:11:49,476
I don't have my phone. I think
I left my phone in the...

233
00:11:50,244 --> 00:11:51,845
In the car.

234
00:11:51,879 --> 00:11:53,013
I gotta... I think it's here.

235
00:11:53,047 --> 00:11:55,716
<i>♪ To sing this song?</i>

236
00:11:55,749 --> 00:11:59,019
<i>♪ How long</i>

237
00:11:59,053 --> 00:12:02,524
<i>♪ To sing this song?</i>

238
00:12:02,557 --> 00:12:05,826
<i>♪ How long?</i>

239
00:12:05,859 --> 00:12:09,163
<i>♪ How long?</i>

240
00:12:09,196 --> 00:12:12,601
<i>♪ How long?</i>

241
