414
00:20:15,750 --> 00:20:16,918
with a heavy heart,

415
00:20:16,951 --> 00:20:18,086
Jim is cashin' in.

416
00:20:18,119 --> 00:20:20,888
He wants to spend more time
with his family.

417
00:20:22,623 --> 00:20:23,624
And apparently,

418
00:20:23,658 --> 00:20:26,828
Audio Adrenaline is
calling it quits, too

419
00:20:26,861 --> 00:20:29,897
because Mark's voice can't
take the abuse anymore.

420
00:20:30,363 --> 00:20:31,899
-So...
-(SIGHS)

421
00:20:31,933 --> 00:20:35,435
...it seems we find ourselves
at the crossroads.

422
00:20:35,469 --> 00:20:39,941
One band member down
and no headliner.

423
00:20:39,974 --> 00:20:41,642
So where does that leave us?

424
00:20:41,676 --> 00:20:42,877
We're alone.

425
00:20:43,678 --> 00:20:44,879
Utterly alone.

426
00:20:44,912 --> 00:20:47,347
Well, that was what you call
a rhetorical question, Nathan,

427
00:20:47,380 --> 00:20:48,916
but thank you.

428
00:20:48,950 --> 00:20:50,752
Now the silver linin' here is

429
00:20:50,785 --> 00:20:53,286
that now you boys are
the headliner.

430
00:20:53,320 --> 00:20:54,488
(CHUCKLES)

431
00:20:54,522 --> 00:20:57,390
<i>Imagine</i> has had
more lives than a stray cat.

432
00:20:57,424 --> 00:21:02,063
But record sales have not
exactly been stellar

433
00:21:02,096 --> 00:21:03,564
as of late.

434
00:21:03,598 --> 00:21:05,499
And we haven't had
a hit single

435
00:21:05,533 --> 00:21:06,934
in quite a while now.

436
00:21:08,069 --> 00:21:09,704
So the question is

437
00:21:11,205 --> 00:21:13,373
are we headliner material?

438
00:21:17,845 --> 00:21:20,982
And I am open
to any new ideas, fellas.

439
00:21:22,150 --> 00:21:24,417
MIKE: He's talking
about you, Bart.

440
00:21:24,451 --> 00:21:28,355
You got another hit cookin'?
It'd be good timing.

441
00:21:29,322 --> 00:21:30,658
He's got nothin'.
You don't have anything?

442
00:21:30,691 --> 00:21:32,093
-He's got nothing.
-Very helpful, Mike.

443
00:21:32,126 --> 00:21:33,293
-Thank you.
-Yep.

444
00:21:33,326 --> 00:21:35,763
Um, if we're headlining,
who's the opening act?

445
00:21:38,365 --> 00:21:40,535
Hi. Um...

446
00:21:40,568 --> 00:21:41,702
I don't know
who needs to hear this,

447
00:21:41,736 --> 00:21:44,105
but I think, uh,
your bus is on fire.

448
00:21:44,138 --> 00:21:46,339
-(GASPS) Oh, no.
-No, I'm kidding.

449
00:21:46,373 --> 00:21:47,575
(CHUCKLES SOFTLY) I'm kidding.

450
00:21:47,608 --> 00:21:49,544
Um, but I did hear
that that happened once.

451
00:21:49,577 --> 00:21:52,213
It was the incense.
It helps me unwind.

452
00:21:52,246 --> 00:21:53,480
I am sorry about that.

453
00:21:53,514 --> 00:21:56,984
Boys, this is Tim Timmons.
He's your opening act.

454
00:21:57,018 --> 00:21:58,820
-Tim, MercyMe.
-TIM: Wow, guys.

455
00:21:58,853 --> 00:22:01,756
It is so good for you
to meet me.

456
00:22:01,789 --> 00:22:03,558
Okay. That's new.

457
00:22:03,591 --> 00:22:05,325
Are there any snacks?

458
00:22:05,358 --> 00:22:06,661
(CHATTERING INDISTINCTLY)

459
00:22:06,694 --> 00:22:08,095
-Thank you so much.
-Pick out your bunk, bro.

460
00:22:08,129 --> 00:22:09,396
-Hey, great.
-Yeah.

461
00:22:09,429 --> 00:22:10,463
-I'm gonna be back for that.
-Okay.

462
00:22:10,497 --> 00:22:12,266
Life of the party.

463
00:22:12,300 --> 00:22:14,635
Oh, he's a barrel
full of monkeys, isn't he?

464
00:22:15,203 --> 00:22:16,737
I'm not sure I like him.

465
00:22:16,771 --> 00:22:19,907
Well, the folks
at the homeless shelter
he works with seem to.

466
00:22:19,941 --> 00:22:23,311
Of course he works
with a homeless shelter.

467
00:22:23,343 --> 00:22:25,980
