your sense of humor,

468
00:22:26,013 --> 00:22:28,015
which I find disquieting.

469
00:22:31,252 --> 00:22:33,154
(BART SIGHS)

470
00:22:33,187 --> 00:22:35,455
I know that look, Brick.
What's up, man?

471
00:22:35,488 --> 00:22:36,924
Shannon called me.

472
00:22:37,825 --> 00:22:39,060
She's worried.

473
00:22:40,493 --> 00:22:42,196
So am I. I mean,

474
00:22:42,230 --> 00:22:46,334
I'm not sure this whole
duct-taped-together tour
thing's gonna work anyhow.

475
00:22:46,366 --> 00:22:47,635
Maybe you stay home
for a while,

476
00:22:47,668 --> 00:22:48,836
writing or something,
you know.

477
00:22:48,870 --> 00:22:51,839
Your family needs you,
Shannon needs you.

478
00:22:51,873 --> 00:22:53,541
Sam, especially.

479
00:22:53,574 --> 00:22:56,277
I don't know, man.
It's just... It's hard.

480
00:22:56,310 --> 00:22:57,778
Why's it got to be so hard?

481
00:22:58,378 --> 00:22:59,647
Which part?

482
00:23:00,848 --> 00:23:01,916
All of it.

483
00:23:03,317 --> 00:23:04,819
Come on, man.

484
00:23:05,853 --> 00:23:08,421
You got your dream.

485
00:23:08,455 --> 00:23:10,858
You inspired
millions of people.

486
00:23:10,892 --> 00:23:12,459
I mean, what did you think
was gonna happen?

487
00:23:12,492 --> 00:23:14,962
You're just gonna ride off
into the sunset?

488
00:23:14,996 --> 00:23:17,765
No more struggles or pain?

489
00:23:17,798 --> 00:23:19,600
